script = ExtResource("1_s")
id = "forge"
display_name = "The Forge"
title = "The Forge"
category = "Resources"
order = 30
image = "res://art/guide/forge.png"
body = "In the Hold, beside the stash. Wood, ore and a gem go in; a piece of gear comes out.

The wood and the ore decide how good a piece the forge may attempt at all - better stock, higher level. The gem decides how often the piece climbs a rung of rarity, and your Smith adds to that. The screen shows you the odds before you spend anything.

A gem is a chance rather than a promise. A Duskstone gives you four attempts at a good rung and can still hand you something ordinary - the rarest gear in the game is found on the road, not made at an anvil, and the forge is deliberately unable to beat it.

Everything the forge makes is rolled on the same tables a drop is. It is another way onto the ladder, never a way past it."
